From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-ipq5018: keep the NSS core clock enabled

Keep the clock branch left running by the bootloader until the NSS driver
takes ownership. Gating it in clk_disable_unused() and re-enabling it at
NSS probe breaks wireless offload on IPQ5018; this is reproducible with WPA2
clients on the GL-B3000. Preserve this one branch rather than globally
disabling unused-clock cleanup.

Backport of the IPQ50xx NSS bring-up fix from kuncy7/openwrt-nss-edma.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq5018.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq5018.c
@@ -2881,7 +2881,7 @@ static struct clk_branch gcc_ubi0_core_clk = {
 				&ubi0_core_clk_src.clkr.hw,
 			},
 			.num_parents = 1,
-			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
+			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED,
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
 		},
 	},
